

relation Type_alpha: ``typeIR''''`` and ``typeIR'''''``

. If ``typeIR''''`` has type ``baseTypeIR``
 .. Let ``baseTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''''``
 .. Check that ``typeIR'''''`` has type ``baseTypeIR``
 .. Let ``baseTypeIR'`` be ``typeIR'''''``
 .. Check that ``baseTypeIR`` is equal to ``baseTypeIR'``
 .. Group basetype: ``baseTypeIR`` and ``baseTypeIR``

  ... The relation holds

. Else if ``typeIR''''`` has type ``nameTypeIR``
 .. Let ``TID tid`` be ``typeIR''''``
 .. Check that ``typeIR'''''`` has type ``nameTypeIR``
 .. Let ``TID tid'`` be ``typeIR'''''``
 .. Check that ``tid`` is equal to ``tid'``
 .. Group nametype: ``TID tid`` and ``TID tid``

  ... The relation holds

. Else if ``typeIR''''`` has type ``specializedTypeIR``
 .. Let ``polyTypeDefIR~a~ < typeIR~a~* >`` be ``typeIR''''``
 .. Check that ``typeIR'''''`` has type ``specializedTypeIR``
 .. Let ``polyTypeDefIR~b~ < typeIR~b~* >`` be ``typeIR'''''``
 .. Group spectype: ``polyTypeDefIR~a~ < typeIR~a~* >`` and ``polyTypeDefIR~b~ < typeIR~b~* >``

  ... Let ``typeIR~a_spec~`` be ``$specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR~a~, typeIR~a~*)``
  ... Let ``typeIR~b_spec~`` be ``$specialize_typeDef(polyTypeDefIR~b~, typeIR~b~*)``
  ... If [``typeIR~a_spec~`` and ``typeIR~b_spec~`` are the same type](Type_alpha), then
   .... If ``$is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~a_spec~) /\ $is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~b_spec~)``
    ..... If [``typeIR~a~`` and ``typeIR~b~`` are the same type](Type_alpha), for each ``typeIR_a`` in ``typeIR_a*`` and ``typeIR_b`` in ``typeIR_b*``, then
     ...... The relation holds
   .... If ``~$is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~a_spec~) /\ ~$is_nominal_typeIR(typeIR~b_spec~)``
    ..... The relation holds
