relation Expr_ok: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``expression'''``

. If ``expression'''`` has type ``booleanLiteral``
 .. Let ``booleanLiteral`` be ``expression'''``
 .. Group literalExpression-boolean: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``booleanLiteral``

  ... If let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( BOOL LCTK )``
   .... Result in ``TRUE # expressionNoteIR``

  ... Else if let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( BOOL LCTK )``
   .... Result in ``FALSE # expressionNoteIR``

. Else if ``expression'''`` has type ``numberLiteral``
 .. Let ``numberLiteral`` be ``expression'''``
 .. Group literalExpression-number: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``numberLiteral``

  ... If let ``D i`` be ``numberLiteral``
   .... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( INT LCTK )``
   .... Result in ``D i # expressionNoteIR``

  ... Else if let ``n S i`` be ``numberLiteral``
   .... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( INT < n > LCTK )``
   .... Result in ``n S i # expressionNoteIR``

  ... Else if let ``n W i`` be ``numberLiteral``
   .... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( BIT < n > LCTK )``
   .... Result in ``n W i # expressionNoteIR``

. Else if ``expression'''`` has type ``stringLiteral``
 .. Let ``" text "`` be ``expression'''``
 .. Group literalExpression-stringLiteral: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``" text "``

  ... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( STRING LCTK )``
  ... Result in ``" text " # expressionNoteIR``
. Group referenceExpression: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``expression``

 .. If ``expression'''`` has type ``prefixedNonTypeName``
  ... Let ``prefixedNonTypeName`` be ``expression'''``
  ... Let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``$prefixedNonTypeName(prefixedNonTypeName)``
  ... Let ``varTypeIR?`` be ``$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)``
  ... Check that ``varTypeIR?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
  ... Let ``?(_ typeIR ctk _?)`` be ``varTypeIR``?
  ... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( typeIR ctk )``
  ... Result in ``prefixedNameIR # expressionNoteIR``
 .. If ``THIS`` is equal to ``expression'''``
  ... Let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``` "this"``
  ... Let ``varTypeIR?`` be ``$find_var(p, TC, prefixedNameIR)``
  ... Check that ``varTypeIR?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
  ... Let ``?(_ typeIR ctk _?)`` be ``varTypeIR``?
  ... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( typeIR ctk )``
  ... Result in ``prefixedNameIR # expressionNoteIR``
. If ``expression'''`` has type ``defaultExpression``
 .. Let ``defaultExpression`` be ``expression'''``
 .. Group defaultExpression: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``...``

  ... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( DEFAULT LCTK )``
  ... Result in ``... # expressionNoteIR``

. Else if ``expression'''`` has type ``unaryExpression``
 .. Let ``unop expression`` be ``expression'''``
 .. If ``unop`` matches pattern ``!``


 .. Else if ``unop`` matches pattern ``~``

 .. Group unaryExpression-uplusminus: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``unop expression``

  ... If ``unop`` matches pattern ``+``
   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR'?`` be ``$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)``
   .... Check that ``typedExpressionIR'?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
   .... Let ``?(typedExpressionIR~reduced~)`` be ``typedExpressionIR'``?
   .... Let ``typeIR~reduced~`` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  ``typedExpressionIR~reduced~``>>
   .... Let ``ctk~reduced~`` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  ``typedExpressionIR~reduced~``>>
   .... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )``
   .... Result in ``unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR``

  ... Else if ``unop`` matches pattern ``-``
   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR'?`` be ``$reduce_serenum_unary(typedExpressionIR, $compat_uplusminus)``
   .... Check that ``typedExpressionIR'?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
   .... Let ``?(typedExpressionIR~reduced~)`` be ``typedExpressionIR'``?
   .... Let ``typeIR~reduced~`` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  ``typedExpressionIR~reduced~``>>
   .... Let ``ctk~reduced~`` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  ``typedExpressionIR~reduced~``>>
   .... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )``
   .... Result in ``unop typedExpressionIR~reduced~ # expressionNoteIR``

. Else if ``expression'''`` has type ``binaryExpression``
 .. Let ``expression~l~ binop expression~r~`` be ``expression'''``
 .. Group binaryExpression-plusminusmult: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``expression~l~ binop expression~r~``

  ... Check that ``binop`` is in ``[+, -, and *]``
  ... Let ``typedExpressionIR~l~`` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing ``expression~l~``, under cursor ``p`` and typing context ``TC``>>
  ... Let ``typedExpressionIR~r~`` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing ``expression~r~``, under cursor ``p`` and typing context ``TC``>>
  ... Let ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?`` be ``$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)``
  ... Check that ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
  ... Let ``?((typedExpressionIR~l_cast~ and typedExpressionIR~r_cast~))`` be ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)``?
  ... Let ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?`` be ``$reduce_serenum_binary(typedExpressionIR~l_cast~, typedExpressionIR~r_cast~, $compat_plusminusmult)``
  ... Check that ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
  ... Let ``?((typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ and typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~))`` be ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)'``?
  ... Let ``typeIR~reduced~`` be <<typeof_expression, the type of  ``typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~``>>
  ... Let ``ctk~l_reduced~`` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  ``typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~``>>
  ... Let ``ctk~r_reduced~`` be <<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  ``typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~``>>
  ... Let ``ctk~reduced~`` be ``$join_ctk(ctk~l_reduced~, ctk~r_reduced~)``
  ... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be ``( typeIR~reduced~ ctk~reduced~ )``
  ... Result in ``typedExpressionIR~l_reduced~ binop typedExpressionIR~r_reduced~ # expressionNoteIR``
 .. Group binaryExpression-satplusminus: ``p``, ``TC``, and ``expression~l~ binop expression~r~``

  ... Check that ``binop`` is in ``[|+| and |-|]``
  ... Let ``typedExpressionIR~l~`` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing ``expression~l~``, under cursor ``p`` and typing context ``TC``>>
  ... Let ``typedExpressionIR~r~`` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing ``expression~r~``, under cursor ``p`` and typing context ``TC``>>
  ... Let ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?`` be ``$coerce_binary(typedExpressionIR~l~, typedExpressionIR~r~)``
  ... Check that ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
  ... Let ``?((typedExpressionIR~l_cast~ and typedExpressionIR~r_cast~))`` be ``(typedExpressionIR, typedExpressionIR)``?
