    ..... Result in ``TBLC~1~`` and ``tablePropertyIR``
  ... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$tableCustomName(tableCustomName)``
  ... If ``nameIR =/= "size" /\ nameIR =/= "largest_priority_wins" /\ nameIR =/= "priority_delta"``
   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR`` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing ``expression``, under cursor ``LOCAL`` and typing context ``TC``>>
   .... Let ``constOptIR`` be ``$flatten_constOpt(constOpt)``
   .... Let ``tablePropertyIR`` be ``annotationList constOptIR CUSTOM nameIR = typedExpressionIR ;``
   .... Result in ``TBLC~0'~`` and ``tablePropertyIR``

relation TableProperties_ok: ``TC``, ``TBLC'``, and ``tableProperty``*

. If ``tableProperty*`` matches pattern ``[]``


. Else if let ``tableProperty~h~ :: tableProperty~t~*`` be ``tableProperty``*
 .. Group cons: ``TC``, ``TBLC~0~``, and ``tableProperty~h~ :: tableProperty~t~*``

  ... (TableProperty_ok: ``TC TBLC' |- tableProperty~h~ : TBLC~1~ tablePropertyIR~h~``)
  ... (TableProperties_ok: ``TC TBLC~1~ |- tableProperty~t~* : TBLC~2~ tablePropertyIR~t~*``)
  ... Result in ``TBLC~2~`` and ``tablePropertyIR~h~ :: tablePropertyIR~t~*``

relation Table_ok: ``TC`` and ``tableProperty``*

. Group : ``TC`` and ``tableProperty``*

 .. Check that ``$count_table_keys(tableProperty*)`` is less than or equal to 1
 .. Check that ``$count_table_actions(tableProperty*)`` is equal to 1
 .. Let ``TBLC~0~`` be ``$empty_tableContext``
 .. (TableProperties_ok: ``TC TBLC~0~ |- tableProperty* : TBLC~1~ tablePropertyIR*``)
 .. Result in ``TBLC~1~`` and ``tablePropertyIR*``

relation TableType_ok: ``TC~0~``, ``TBLC``, and ``name``

. Group : ``TC~0~``, ``TBLC``, and ``name``

 .. Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
 .. Let ``tid~enum~`` be ``"action_list(" ++ nameIR ++ ")"``
 .. Let ``(prefixedNameIR~action~, _*, and _)*`` be ``TBLC.ACTIONS``
 .. Let ``id_enum_field*`` be the list of ``id_enum_field``, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let ``id~enum_field~`` be ``$flatten_prefixedNameIR(prefixedNameIR~action~)``
 .. for each ``prefixedNameIR_action`` in ``prefixedNameIR_action*``
 .. Let ``typeIR~table_enum~`` be ``TABLE_ENUM tid~enum~ { id~enum_field~* }``
 .. Let ``value_enum_field*`` be the list of ``value_enum_field``, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let ``value~enum_field~`` be ``TABLE_ENUM tid~enum~ . id~enum_field~``
 .. for each ``id_enum_field`` in ``id_enum_field*``
 .. Let ``varTypeIR_enum_field*`` be the list of ``varTypeIR_enum_field``, obtained by repeating:
  ... Let ``varTypeIR~enum_field~`` be ``typeIR~table_enum~ LCTK ?(value~enum_field~)``
 .. for each ``value_enum_field`` in ``value_enum_field*``
 .. Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_vars(BLOCK, TC~0~, tid~enum~ ++ "." ++ id~enum_field~*, varTypeIR~enum_field~*)``
 .. Let ``tid~struct~`` be ``"apply_result(" ++ nameIR ++ ")"``
 .. Let ``typeIR~table_struct~`` be ``TABLE_STRUCT tid~struct~ { [BOOL "hit" ;, BOOL "miss" ;, and typeIR~table_enum~ "action_run" ;] }``
 .. Let ``typeIR~table~`` be ``TABLE nameIR # typeIR~table_struct~``
 .. Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``typeIR~table~``

relation ControlLocalDecl_ok: ``TC~0~`` and ``controlLocalDeclaration``

. If ``controlLocalDeclaration`` has type ``constantDeclaration``
 .. Let ``constantDeclaration`` be ``controlLocalDeclaration``
 .. Group constantDeclaration: ``TC~0~`` and ``constantDeclaration``

  ... Let ``TC~1~`` and ``declarationIR`` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing ``constantDeclaration``, under cursor ``BLOCK`` and typing context ``TC~0~``,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that ``declarationIR`` has type ``constantDeclarationIR``
  ... Let ``constantDeclarationIR`` be ``declarationIR``
  ... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``constantDeclarationIR``

. Else if ``controlLocalDeclaration`` has type ``instantiation``
 .. Let ``instantiation`` be ``controlLocalDeclaration``
 .. Group instantiation: ``TC~0~`` and ``instantiation``

  ... Let ``TC~1~`` and ``declarationIR`` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing ``instantiation``, under cursor ``BLOCK`` and typing context ``TC~0~``,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that ``declarationIR`` has type ``instantiationIR``
  ... Let ``instantiationIR`` be ``declarationIR``
  ... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``instantiationIR``

. Else if ``controlLocalDeclaration`` has type ``variableDeclaration``
 .. Let ``annotationList type name initializerOpt ;`` be ``controlLocalDeclaration``
 .. Group variableDeclaration: ``TC~0~`` and ``annotationList type name initializerOpt ;``

  ... If ``initializerOpt`` matches pattern ```EMPTY``
   .... Let ``typeIR`` and ``tid*`` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing ``type``, under cursor ``BLOCK`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
   .... Check that ``tid*`` matches pattern ``[]``
   .... If (Type_wf: ``$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~) |- typeIR``), then
    ..... Check that ``$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)``
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_var(BLOCK, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())``
    ..... Let ``variableDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR nameIR ?() ;``
    ..... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``variableDeclarationIR``
  ... If ``initializerOpt`` has type ``initializer``
   .... Let ``= expression~init~`` be ``initializerOpt``
   .... Let ``typeIR`` and ``tid*`` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing ``type``, under cursor ``BLOCK`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
   .... Check that ``tid*`` matches pattern ``[]``
   .... If (Type_wf: ``$bound(BLOCK, TC~0~) |- typeIR``), then
    ..... Check that ``$is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)``
    ..... Let ``typedExpressionIR~init~`` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing ``expression~init~``, under cursor ``BLOCK`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
    ..... Let ``typedExpressionIR?`` be ``$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~init~, typeIR)``
    ..... Check that ``typedExpressionIR?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
    ..... Let ``?(typedExpressionIR~init_cast~)`` be ``typedExpressionIR``?
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_var(BLOCK, TC~0~, nameIR, INOUT typeIR DYN ?())``
    ..... Let ``variableDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR nameIR ?(= typedExpressionIR~init_cast~) ;``
    ..... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``variableDeclarationIR``

. Else if ``controlLocalDeclaration`` has type ``actionDeclaration``
 .. Let ``actionDeclaration`` be ``controlLocalDeclaration``
 .. Group actionDeclaration: ``TC~0~`` and ``actionDeclaration``

  ... Let ``TC~1~`` and ``declarationIR`` be the result of <<Decl_ok, typing ``actionDeclaration``, under cursor ``BLOCK`` and typing context ``TC~0~``,
and the modified typing context>>
  ... Check that ``declarationIR`` has type ``actionDeclarationIR``
  ... Let ``actionDeclarationIR`` be ``declarationIR``
  ... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``actionDeclarationIR``

. Else if ``controlLocalDeclaration`` has type ``tableDeclaration``
 .. Let ``annotationList TABLE name { tablePropertyList }`` be ``controlLocalDeclaration``
 .. Group tableDeclaration: ``TC~0~`` and ``annotationList TABLE name { tablePropertyList }``

  ... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``TC~0~``[LOCAL.KIND = ``TABLE_APPLY_METHOD``]
  ... Let ``tableProperty*`` be ``$flatten_tablePropertyList(tablePropertyList)``
  ... (Table_ok: ``TC~1~ |- tableProperty* : TBLC tablePropertyIR*``)
  ... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
  ... (TableType_ok: ``TC~1~ TBLC |- name : TC~2~ typeIR~table~``)
  ... Let ``TC~3~`` be ``$add_var(BLOCK, TC~2~, nameIR, typeIR~table~ DYN ?())``
  ... Let ``tableDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList TABLE typeIR~table~ nameIR { tablePropertyIR* }``
  ... Result in ``TC~3~`` and ``tableDeclarationIR``

relation ControlLocalDecls_ok: ``TC'`` and ``controlLocalDeclaration``*

. If ``controlLocalDeclaration*`` matches pattern ``[]``


. Else if let ``controlLocalDeclaration~h~ :: controlLocalDeclaration~t~*`` be ``controlLocalDeclaration``*
 .. Group cons: ``TC~0~`` and ``controlLocalDeclaration~h~ :: controlLocalDeclaration~t~*``

  ... (ControlLocalDecl_ok: ``TC' |- controlLocalDeclaration~h~ : TC~1~ controlLocalDeclarationIR~h~``)
  ... (ControlLocalDecls_ok: ``TC~1~ |- controlLocalDeclaration~t~* : TC~2~ controlLocalDeclarationIR~t~*``)
  ... Result in ``TC~2~`` and ``controlLocalDeclarationIR~h~ :: controlLocalDeclarationIR~t~*``

relation Decl_ok: ``p'``, ``TC~0~``, and ``declaration``

. If ``declaration`` has type ``constantDeclaration``
 .. Let ``annotationList CONST type name = expression~value~ ;`` be ``declaration``
 .. Group constantDeclaration: ``p``, ``TC~0~``, and ``annotationList CONST type name = expression~value~ ;``

  ... Let ``typeIR`` and ``tid*`` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing ``type``, under cursor ``p'`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
  ... Check that ``tid*`` matches pattern ``[]``
  ... If (Type_wf: ``$bound(p', TC~0~) |- typeIR``), then
   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR~value~`` be the result of <<Expr_ok, typing ``expression~value~``, under cursor ``p'`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
   .... Check that ``<<ctkof_expression, the compile-time known-ness of  typedExpressionIR~value~>>`` matches pattern ``LCTK``
   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR?`` be ``$coerce_unary(typedExpressionIR~value~, typeIR)``
   .... Check that ``typedExpressionIR?`` matches pattern ``(_)``
   .... Let ``?(typedExpressionIR~value_cast~)`` be ``typedExpressionIR``?
   .... Let ``value`` be the result of <<Eval_static, the static evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~value_cast~``, under cursor ``p'`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
   .... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
   .... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR LCTK ?(value))``
   .... Let ``constantDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList CONST typeIR nameIR = value ;``
   .... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``constantDeclarationIR``

. Else if ``declaration`` has type ``instantiation``
 .. Let ``instantiation`` be ``declaration``
 .. If let ``annotationList type ( argumentList ) name ;`` be ``instantiation``
  ... Group instantiation-non-objectInitializer: ``p``, ``TC~0~``, and ``annotationList type ( argumentList ) name ;``

   .... If ``type`` has type ``prefixedTypeName``
    ..... Let ``prefixedTypeName`` be ``type``
    ..... Let ``argument*`` be ``$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)``
    ..... Let ``argumentIR*`` be the list of ``argumentIR``, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let ``argumentIR`` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing ``argument``, under cursor ``p'`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
    ..... for each ``argument`` in ``argument*``
    ..... Let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)``
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: ``p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < [] > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~impl~* > ( # id~default~* )``)
    ..... (Inst_ok: ``p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < [] # tid~impl~* > ( argumentIR* # id~default~* ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR~cast~* )``)
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object~ CTK ?())``
    ..... Let ``instantiationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR~object~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?() ;``
    ..... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``instantiationIR``

   .... Else if ``type`` has type ``specializedType``
    ..... Let ``prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >`` be ``type``
    ..... Let ``typeArgument*`` be ``$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)``
    ..... (TypeArguments_ok: ``p' TC~0~ |- typeArgument* : typeArgumentIR* # tid~impl~*``)
    ..... Let ``argument*`` be ``$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)``
    ..... Let ``argumentIR*`` be the list of ``argumentIR``, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let ``argumentIR`` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing ``argument``, under cursor ``p'`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
    ..... for each ``argument`` in ``argument*``
    ..... Let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)``
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: ``p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~inserted~* > ( # id~default~* )``)
    ..... Let ``tid~infer~*`` be ``tid~impl~* ++ tid~inserted~*``
    ..... (Inst_ok: ``p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR* # tid~infer~* > ( argumentIR* # id~default~* ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR~cast~* )``)
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object~ CTK ?())``
    ..... Let ``instantiationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR~object~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?() ;``
    ..... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``instantiationIR``

 .. Else if let ``annotationList type ( argumentList ) name = { objectDeclarationList } ;`` be ``instantiation``
  ... Group instantiation-objectInitializer: ``p``, ``TC~0~``, and ``annotationList type ( argumentList ) name = { objectDeclarationList } ;``

   .... If ``type`` has type ``prefixedTypeName``
    ..... Let ``prefixedTypeName`` be ``type``
    ..... Let ``argument*`` be ``$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)``
    ..... Let ``argumentIR*`` be the list of ``argumentIR``, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let ``argumentIR`` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing ``argument``, under cursor ``p'`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
    ..... for each ``argument`` in ``argument*``
    ..... Let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)``
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: ``p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < [] > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~impl~* > ( # id~default~* )``)
    ..... (Inst_ok: ``p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < [] # tid~impl~* > ( argumentIR* # id~default~* ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR~cast~* )``)
    ..... Check that ``$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR~object~>>)``
    ..... Check that ``typeIR~object~`` has type ``specializedTypeIR``
    ..... Let ``typeIR < tid~expl~* , tid'* > < typeIR~arg~* >`` be ``typeIR~object~``
    ..... Check that ``typeIR`` has type ``externObjectTypeIR``
    ..... Let ``EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~extern~`` be ``typeIR``
    ..... Check that ``tid'``* is equal to ``tid~impl~``*
    ..... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, "this", typeIR~object~ CTK ?())``
    ..... Let ``objectDeclaration*`` be ``$flatten_objectDeclarationList(objectDeclarationList)``
    ..... (Decls_object_ok: ``p' TC~1~ { [] } { [] } |- objectDeclaration* : frame~init~ rdenv~init~ objectDeclarationIR*``)
    ..... Let ``tid*`` be ``tid~expl~* ++ tid~impl~*``
    ..... Let ``theta`` be ``{ tid : typeIR~arg~* }``
    ..... Let ``rdenv~init_subst~`` be ``$subst_rdenv(theta, rdenv~extern~, rdenv~init~)``
    ..... Let ``typeIR~object_init~`` be ``EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~init_subst~ < tid~expl~* , tid~impl~* > < typeIR~arg~* >``
    ..... Check that ``$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object_init~)``
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``TC~2~`` be ``$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object_init~ CTK ?())``
    ..... Let ``instantiationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR~object_init~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?(= { objectDeclarationIR* }) ;``
    ..... Result in ``TC~2~`` and ``instantiationIR``

   .... Else if ``type`` has type ``specializedType``
    ..... Let ``prefixedTypeName < typeArgumentList >`` be ``type``
    ..... Let ``typeArgument*`` be ``$flatten_typeArgumentList(typeArgumentList)``
    ..... (TypeArguments_ok: ``p' TC~0~ |- typeArgument* : typeArgumentIR* # tid~impl~*``)
    ..... Let ``argument*`` be ``$flatten_argumentList(argumentList)``
    ..... Let ``argumentIR*`` be the list of ``argumentIR``, obtained by repeating:
     ...... Let ``argumentIR`` be the result of <<Argument_ok, typing ``argument``, under cursor ``p'`` and typing context ``TC~0~``>>
    ..... for each ``argument`` in ``argument*``
    ..... Let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``$prefixedTypeName(prefixedTypeName)``
    ..... (ConstructorType_ok: ``p' TC~0~ |- prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR* > ( argumentIR* ) : constructorTypeIR < # tid~inserted~* > ( # id~default~* )``)
    ..... Let ``tid~infer~*`` be ``tid~impl~* ++ tid~inserted~*``
    ..... (Inst_ok: ``p' TC~0~ NAMED |- constructorTypeIR < typeArgumentIR* # tid~infer~* > ( argumentIR* # id~default~* ) : typeIR~object~ < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR~cast~* )``)
    ..... Check that ``$is_extern_object_typeIR(<<canon, the canonicalized form of typeIR~object~>>)``
    ..... Check that ``typeIR~object~`` has type ``specializedTypeIR``
    ..... Let ``typeIR < tid~expl~* , tid'* > < typeIR~arg~* >`` be ``typeIR~object~``
    ..... Check that ``typeIR`` has type ``externObjectTypeIR``
    ..... Let ``EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~extern~`` be ``typeIR``
    ..... Check that ``tid'``* is equal to ``tid~impl~``*
    ..... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_var(LOCAL, TC~0~, "this", typeIR~object~ CTK ?())``
    ..... Let ``objectDeclaration*`` be ``$flatten_objectDeclarationList(objectDeclarationList)``
    ..... (Decls_object_ok: ``p' TC~1~ { [] } { [] } |- objectDeclaration* : frame~init~ rdenv~init~ objectDeclarationIR*``)
    ..... Let ``tid*`` be ``tid~expl~* ++ tid~impl~*``
    ..... Let ``theta`` be ``{ tid : typeIR~arg~* }``
    ..... Let ``rdenv~init_subst~`` be ``$subst_rdenv(theta, rdenv~extern~, rdenv~init~)``
    ..... Let ``typeIR~object_init~`` be ``EXTERN tid~extern~ rdenv~init_subst~ < tid~expl~* , tid~impl~* > < typeIR~arg~* >``
    ..... Check that ``$is_concrete_extern_object(typeIR~object_init~)``
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``TC~2~`` be ``$add_var(p', TC~0~, nameIR, typeIR~object_init~ CTK ?())``
    ..... Let ``instantiationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR~object_init~ prefixedNameIR < typeArgumentIR~inferred~* > ( argumentIR* ) nameIR ?(= { objectDeclarationIR* }) ;``
    ..... Result in ``TC~2~`` and ``instantiationIR``

. Else if ``declaration`` has type ``functionDeclaration``
 .. Let ``annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement`` be ``declaration``
 .. Group functionDeclaration: ``p``, ``TC~0~``, and ``annotationList typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) blockStatement``

  ... Let ``typeParameter*`` be ``$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)``
  ... Let ``tid_expl*`` be the list of ``tid_expl``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``tid~expl~`` be ``$name(typeParameter)``
  ... for each ``typeParameter`` in ``typeParameter*``
  ... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_types(LOCAL, TC~0~, tid~expl~*, TID tid~expl~*)``
  ... Let ``typeIR~ret~`` and ``tid*`` be the result of <<Type_ok, typing ``typeOrVoid``, under cursor ``LOCAL`` and typing context ``TC~1~``>>
  ... Check that ``tid*`` matches pattern ``[]``
  ... Let ``parameter*`` be ``$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)``
  ... Let ``parameterIR*`` and ``tid~impl~*`` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing ``parameter*``, under cursor ``LOCAL`` and typing context ``TC~1~``>>
  ... Let ``parameterTypeIR*`` be the list of ``parameterTypeIR``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``parameterTypeIR`` be ``$parameterIR(parameterIR)``
  ... for each ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR*``
  ... Let ``TC~2~`` be ``$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~1~, parameterTypeIR*)``
  ... Let ``TC~3~`` be ``TC~2~``[LOCAL.KIND = ``FUNCTION -> typeIR~ret~``]
  ... (Block_ok: ``TC~3~ CONT |- blockStatement : _ f blockStatementIR``)
  ... If ``f`` matches pattern ``RET``
   .... Let ``rid`` be ``$rid(name, parameterList)``
   .... Let ``functionTypeIR`` be ``FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR~ret~``
   .... Let ``routineTypeDefIR`` be ``functionTypeIR < tid~expl~* , tid~impl~* >``
   .... If (RoutineTypeDef_wf: ``$bound(p', TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR``), then
    ..... Let ``TC~4~`` be ``$add_routine_overload(p', TC~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)``
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``functionDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~* , tid~impl~* > ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR``
    ..... Result in ``TC~4~`` and ``functionDeclarationIR``
  ... If ``typeIR~ret~`` is equal to ``VOID``
   .... Let ``rid`` be ``$rid(name, parameterList)``
   .... Let ``functionTypeIR`` be ``FUNCTION ( parameterTypeIR* ) -> typeIR~ret~``
   .... Let ``routineTypeDefIR`` be ``functionTypeIR < tid~expl~* , tid~impl~* >``
   .... If (RoutineTypeDef_wf: ``$bound(p', TC~0~) |- routineTypeDefIR``), then
    ..... Let ``TC~4~`` be ``$add_routine_overload(p', TC~0~, rid, routineTypeDefIR)``
    ..... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
    ..... Let ``functionDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR~ret~ nameIR < tid~expl~* , tid~impl~* > ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR``
    ..... Result in ``TC~4~`` and ``functionDeclarationIR``

. Else if ``declaration`` has type ``actionDeclaration``
 .. Let ``annotationList ACTION name ( parameterList ) blockStatement`` be ``declaration``
 .. Group actionDeclaration: ``p``, ``TC~0~``, and ``annotationList ACTION name ( parameterList ) blockStatement``

  ... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``TC~0~``[LOCAL.KIND = ``ACTION``]
  ... Let ``parameter*`` be ``$flatten_parameterList(parameterList)``
  ... Let ``parameterIR*`` and ``tid*`` be the result of <<Parameters_ok, typing ``parameter*``, under cursor ``LOCAL`` and typing context ``TC~1~``>>
  ... Check that ``tid*`` matches pattern ``[]``
  ... Let ``parameterTypeIR*`` be the list of ``parameterTypeIR``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``parameterTypeIR`` be ``$parameterIR(parameterIR)``
  ... for each ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR*``
  ... Let ``TC~2~`` be ``$add_parameters(LOCAL, TC~1~, parameterTypeIR*)``
  ... (Block_ok: ``TC~2~ CONT |- blockStatement : _ _ blockStatementIR``)
  ... Let ``rid`` be ``$rid(name, parameterList)``
  ... Let ``functionTypeIR`` be ``ACTION ( parameterTypeIR* )``
  ... If (RoutineTypeDef_wf: ``$bound(p', TC~0~) |- functionTypeIR``), then
   .... Let ``TC~3~`` be ``$add_routine_non_overload(p', TC~0~, rid, functionTypeIR)``
   .... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
   .... Let ``actionDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList ACTION nameIR ( parameterIR* ) blockStatementIR``
   .... Result in ``TC~3~`` and ``actionDeclarationIR``
. Check that ``p'`` matches pattern ``GLOBAL``
. If ``declaration`` has type ``errorDeclaration``
 .. Let ``ERROR { nameList }`` be ``declaration``
 .. Group errorDeclaration: ``GLOBAL``, ``TC~0~``, and ``ERROR { nameList }``

  ... Let ``name*`` be ``$flatten_nameList(nameList)``
  ... Let ``nameIR*`` be the list of ``nameIR``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
  ... for each ``name`` in ``name*``
  ... Check that ``$distinct_<nameIR>(nameIR*)``
  ... Let ``nameIR_error*`` be the list of ``nameIR_error``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``nameIR~error~`` be ``"error." ++ nameIR``
  ... for each ``nameIR`` in ``nameIR*``
  ... Let ``value_error*`` be the list of ``value_error``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``value~error~`` be ``ERROR . nameIR``
  ... for each ``nameIR`` in ``nameIR*``
  ... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_vars(GLOBAL, TC~0~, nameIR~error~*, ERROR LCTK ?(value~error~)*)``
  ... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``ERROR { nameIR* }``

. Else if ``declaration`` has type ``matchKindDeclaration``
 .. Let ``MATCH_KIND { nameList _ }`` be ``declaration``
 .. Group matchKindDeclaration: ``GLOBAL``, ``TC~0~``, and ``MATCH_KIND { nameList _ }``

  ... Let ``name*`` be ``$flatten_nameList(nameList)``
  ... Let ``nameIR*`` be the list of ``nameIR``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``nameIR`` be ``$name(name)``
  ... for each ``name`` in ``name*``
  ... Check that ``$distinct_<nameIR>(nameIR*)``
  ... Let ``value_match_kind*`` be the list of ``value_match_kind``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``value~match_kind~`` be ``MATCH_KIND . nameIR``
  ... for each ``nameIR`` in ``nameIR*``
  ... Let ``TC~1~`` be ``$add_vars(GLOBAL, TC~0~, nameIR*, MATCH_KIND LCTK ?(value~match_kind~)*)``
  ... Result in ``TC~1~`` and ``MATCH_KIND { nameIR* }``

. Else if ``declaration`` has type ``externFunctionDeclaration``
 .. Let ``annotationList EXTERN typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;`` be ``declaration``
 .. Group externFunctionDeclaration: ``GLOBAL``, ``TC~0~``, and ``annotationList EXTERN typeOrVoid name typeParameterListOpt ( parameterList ) ;``

  ... Let ``typeParameter*`` be ``$flatten_typeParameterListOpt(typeParameterListOpt)``
  ... Let ``tid_expl*`` be the list of ``tid_expl``, obtained by repeating:
   .... Let ``tid~expl~`` be ``$name(typeParameter)``
